# Wake urgency routing: which events wake the model at once, which wait for the next
# turn, and which are only recorded. bin/jg-wake-lib.sh reads it; config/wake-routing
# overrides this file in a home and JG_WAKE_ROUTING overrides both.
#   now     wakes on its own: a captain decision, security, a failed release, a stuck
#           worker past its threshold, a finished task.
#   batch   a durable row that does not wake on its own: it arrives with the next wake of
#           any kind or with the watcher's resurface cadence, so routine events cost one
#           turn between them and none is dropped.
#   silent  recorded only; bin/jg-wake.sh settled reads it.
# A rule is `<class> <kind> <key-glob> <payload-glob>`; the first match wins. kind is
# signal, stale, check, heartbeat, or `*`. A `<task>.status` event is matched against the
# newest line of its status file, so a home rule can hold a routine state word, e.g.
# `batch signal *.status working*`; any other event is matched against its payload. No
# match means `now`, so a missing rule file hides nothing.
set re-alert-minutes 30
# A settled wake is recorded, never queued. Past this many settled wakes in one hour the
# next ones ride the digest as `batch`, so a flood is never hidden. 0 turns the cap off.
set silence-cap-per-hour 30
# How long Main's own restart pass counts as the cause of a relaunch notice.
set restart-pass-seconds 600

# class  kind    key              payload
now      *       *                needs-decision*
now      *       *                failed*
now      *       *                blocked*
now      *       *                done*
batch    signal  *.turn-ended     *
batch    check   merged-*         *
# A board ask that carries no must category is a rule failure, not an alarm: the
# gate routes it to Overwatch and Main answers it there, so it rides the next
# digest instead of waking a model of its own. The two board-gate reports that do
# need a model keep the default: a merge with no proof, and a must ask waiting
# over 48 hours.
now      check   *board-gate.check.sh   *merge landed with no board Evidence card*
now      check   *board-gate.check.sh   *must ask waiting over 48h*
batch    check   *board-gate.check.sh   *board ask*
batch    check   *dpr-green*      *
batch    check   post-merge-ci-*  *
# The tickets checks report board bookkeeping and never ask the captain anything:
# a board row the work has already settled, or a pass summary, is not a decision.
# bin/jg-ticket.sh writes the state where the work happens, so the check that
# reports any remainder rides the next digest instead of waking a model.
batch    check   *tickets-stale.check.sh    *
batch    check   *tickets-sync.check.sh     *
# Wakes that need no model (a class may carry `@condition`; bin/jg-wake-lib.sh owns them):
# a paused home answering a pause, the relaunch Main's own restart pass caused, a
# timer on a paused home, and a re-arm that finds nothing waiting for a turn.
silent@parked        signal  *.status         paused*
silent@parked        check   *                *waiting-state*
silent@restart-pass  check   squad-lead-relaunch-*   *auto-relaunched*
silent@queue-quiet   check   rearm-resurface  *
# A doorbell the watcher deferred because the worker's turn is still running lands by itself
# when the turn ends; the watcher says so in its own words. A doorbell that is still
# unhandled with an idle pane, or a dead endpoint, keeps the default and wakes a model.
silent   stale   *                *unread juggernaut instruction*no interrupt is needed unless the worker is wedged*
now      *       *                *
